 actually  like if you're already working somewhere  it kind of takes a lot of effort to move  somewhere else  and  even if you do that process is going to  take months  so  now you've already wasted months of your  precious internship hours so  try to be pretty selective about it  right from the get-go  and ask a lot of questions during your  interview process  be direct  um  ask about how the firm helps interns  collect their hours  what kind of projects am i going to be  working on do you have like resources  to help me with the exam process and  yeah try to ask those questions even if  it's a little bit awkward  at least that way you've kind of done  your due diligence and you've done your  best to try to figure out what it's like  try to figure out what type of projects  you're going to be working on  [Music]  so the way your hours works is you can  use any project in your office to  collect hours in different categories  like they don't all have to be from one  project  so if you have a  new house that's in schematic design  phase you can use that project to  collect your  site analysis hours and like schematic  design hours  and if you have a project in ca um in  construction min then you can collect uh  ca hours from that particular project  the only problem with that is that  you're really getting like bits and  pieces of information and i think the  best learning experience is actually  if you see a project through  from start to finish  and so therefore i think a small project  will be much better for you like a house  or like a retrofit  because they have shorter time spans and  you can actually see the project through  from like beginning to schematic design  to construction to project closeout in  my office  my project was a small office renault  for the city of coquitlam  and i was a little bit concerned  actually because it's not a new building  so there wasn't any like site work or  like foundations that had to go in  but  what's more  important is 